<Docs slug="select-a-photo">
  <p>
    Highlight a photo in the grid and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> or
    <kbd>Space</kbd> to open it full size in the editor. From there:
  </p>

  <ul class="lp-article-list">
    <li>
      <kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> step to the previous or next photo
      without leaving the editor, so you can move through a burst at full size.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>Esc</kbd> goes back to the grid; <kbd>E</kbd> and <kbd>G</kbd> jump
      between the editor and the library.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>0</kbd> fits the photo to the window,
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>1</kbd> shows it at 1:1, and
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>=</kbd> / <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>-</kbd> zoom in and
      out in steps. Hold <kbd>Space</kbd> and drag to pan, or scroll to move
      around.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>C</kbd> and <kbd>Y</kbd> flip between the original and your edit,
      which is the quickest way to check you have not gone too far.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Picking the best of a burst</h2>
  <p>
    When <a href="/docs/browse.html">Bursts</a> is on, the group wears a badge
    on its first frame. Click the badge to survey the group side by side:
    pick the frame you want and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to keep it, or
    <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close without choosing. Duplicate groups work the same
    way.
  </p>

  <p>
    Once a photo is open, the tabs on the right are where you
    <a href="/docs/adjust.html">adjust the settings</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
